# wear/man/robe: the man's Robe (Imperial, Jade and Starspire men, priests and scholars): one long garment closed left
# over right, the crossed collar trimmed in the trim colour running from the neck across the chest, a sash at the waist
# knotted at his left with its two tails hanging, the skirt to the ankles with a trimmed border (robe_hang), wide sleeves
# flaring at trimmed cuffs (robe_sleeve_*). The trims are the garment's edge (a border or embroidery recolours them).
# The slice (P2b wave 1, FOLK-BODY) drew the first robe; GARB-M (P2b wave 2) redrew it. Fitted to the man (STYLE_P2 22).
# The side run (leg pass round 2, 2026-10-20): the side `run` views (the side run frames take torso=run) are the rest
# views unchanged: this garment covers the legs (or its hang carries the skirt).
# PROTO6 i3 (2026-10-22; the blind panel: the run read as an upright walk): each side `run` view has a `runl` twin that
# the side run frames name (loco.clip torso=runl): the rows from 4 under the neck sit a pixel back and from 7 under it two
# pixels back, so under the clip's lean 4 the chest leads the waist (a real lean; the head never leaves the torso) and the
# hem lands where lean 2 put it, over the run legs; the hip-anchored tails follow it (hip 2, the woman's 3). Walks keep `run`.
use person
legend T pattern 2
legend U pattern 3
body man
role garment robe
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso

